    "created_at": "2020-10-02T13:34:25Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-10-02T13:35:30Z",
    "body": "My use case is for short, silent video clips that \"bounce\" forward and back as an alternative to the loop attribute, by setting the `playbackRate` to -1 in the `onended` handler. While this is currently supported in Safari, it would be great to expect this behavior for the other browsers as well. Not (necessarily) a gimmick, this can be used to create more seamless video loops akin to Instagram's popular Boomerang feature.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
